## PR Title
Fixed calculation of sufficiently_filled when the FIFO is full and aw_requests_remaining is less than a maximum burst

## PR Description
When `aw_requests_remaining` is less than `1 << LGMAXBURST`, the entire `data_available` value should be checked instead of just the lower `data_available[LGMAXBURST-1:0]` slice. In the contributor's case `data_available` was `0x200`, so the slice evaluated to 0 and the transfer never finished. Fixes issue #69.

